---
import Plate from '../../plate/Plate.astro';
import { renderFormula } from '../../../lib/formulas/render';
import { CURVE_SEGMENTS, MINIMUM_DEGREES, PINS } from './math';
import { CUES, FILM_DURATION, formatTime } from './story';
import './curve-budget.css';

const formula = (tex: string) => renderFormula(tex, false);

const escape = (text: string) => text.replaceAll('&', '&amp;').replaceAll('<', '&lt;').replaceAll('>', '&gt;');

function subtitle(text: string): string {
  const pieces = text.split('$');

  return pieces.map((piece, index) => {
    if (index % 2 === 0) return escape(index > 0 ? piece.replace(/^\S+/, '') : piece);

    const attached = /^\S+/.exec(pieces[index + 1] ?? '')?.[0] ?? '';

    return `<span class="nfilm-phrase">${formula(piece)}${escape(attached)}</span>`;
  }).join('');
}

const labels = [
  { id: 'coefficient', tex: 'd^2/2', blue: false },
  { id: 'cost', tex: 'm^2/2', blue: false },
  { id: 'line', tex: String.raw`d=m\sqrt r`, blue: true },
  { id: 'strict', tex: String.raw`d>m\sqrt r`, blue: true },
  { id: 'nine', tex: String.raw`3=1\sqrt9`, blue: false },
  { id: 'old', tex: String.raw`\frac{117}{37}`, blue: false },
  { id: 'root', tex: String.raw`\sqrt{10}\approx3.1623`, blue: true },
  { id: 'remaining', tex: 'r-9', blue: false },
];

const planeX = (x: number) => 150 + x / 1.08 * 124;

const planeY = (y: number) => 150 - y / 1.08 * 124;

const cubicPath = CURVE_SEGMENTS.cubic.map((segment) => `M${planeX(segment.from.x)} ${planeY(segment.from.y)}L${planeX(segment.to.x)} ${planeY(segment.to.y)}`).join('');

const plotX = (m: number) => 45 + m / 8 * 230;

const plotY = (d: number) => 235 - d / 32 * 192;
---

<Plate
  caption="Curves through ten scattered points: why counting coefficients suggests the line d = m√r, why nine points sit on it and ten points must stay above it, and how the approved proof turns that into interpolation one row at a time."
  leftOut="Seshadri constants and the nef class; Hilbert's fourteenth problem; the earlier bounds and cone constructions; the cyclic product, normal polynomial and ruled surface; the interpolation matrix and row-count conditions; the common power of the curve; the SHGH conjecture; the Lean comparator. The proof drawings are schematic."
>
  <uruk-curve-budget>
    <div class="nfilm">
      <div class="nfilm-stage" data-film-viewport>
        <canvas class="nfilm-canvas" data-film-canvas role="img" aria-label="A film about curves through fixed points, the coefficients each point requires, and the degree threshold in Nagata's conjecture. It illustrates the approved proof with a pinched cubic and interpolation. A complete text transcript follows."></canvas>
        <div class="nfilm-still" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="nfilm-still-plane">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 300 300" role="presentation">
              <text x="150" y="15" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink)" font-family="var(--font-special-elite)" font-size="10">A CUBIC THROUGH NINE PINS</text>
              <rect x="26" y="26" width="248" height="248" fill="none" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-opacity=".4" />
              <path d={cubicPath} fill="none" stroke="var(--ink)" stroke-width="1.3" />
              {PINS.map((pin, index) => (
                <>
                  <circle cx={planeX(pin.x)} cy={planeY(pin.y)} r={index === 9 ? 4.5 : 3.5} fill={index === 9 ? 'var(--paper)' : 'var(--ink)'} stroke="var(--ink)" stroke-width="1.2" />
                  <text x={planeX(pin.x) + 10} y={planeY(pin.y) - 8} text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--muted)" font-family="var(--font-special-elite)" font-size="9">{index + 1}</text>
                </>
              ))}
              <text x="150" y="293" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--muted)" font-family="var(--font-alegreya)" font-size="12">Pin 10 is off this curve.</text>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <div class="nfilm-still-plot">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 320 300" role="presentation">
              <defs><pattern id="nfilm-still-hatch" width="7" height="7" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse"><path d="M0 7L7 0" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width=".6" /></pattern></defs>
              <text x="160" y="15" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink)" font-family="var(--font-special-elite)" font-size="10">d: DEGREE OF THE CURVE</text>
              <path d={`M45 235L275 235L275 ${plotY(8 * Math.sqrt(10))}Z`} fill="url(#nfilm-still-hatch)" opacity=".45" />
              <line x1="45" y1="43" x2="45" y2="235" stroke="var(--muted)" />
              <line x1="45" y1="235" x2="275" y2="235" stroke="var(--muted)" />
              <line x1="45" y1="235" x2="275" y2={plotY(8 * Math.sqrt(10))} stroke="var(--blue)" stroke-width="1.5" />
              {[0, 8, 16, 24, 32].map((degree) => <text x="35" y={plotY(degree) + 4} text-anchor="end" fill="var(--muted)" font-family="var(--font-alegreya)" font-size="11">{degree}</text>)}
              {[0, 2, 4, 6, 8].map((m) => <text x={plotX(m)} y="251" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--muted)" font-family="var(--font-alegreya)" font-size="11">{m}</text>)}
              {MINIMUM_DEGREES.map((degree, index) => <circle cx={plotX(index + 1)} cy={plotY(degree)} r="3" fill="var(--ink)" />)}
              <text x="120" y="68" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink)" font-family="var(--font-alegreya)" font-size="12">Solved at these pins</text>
              <text x="205" y="174" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--blue)" font-family="var(--font-alegreya)" font-size="13">d = m√10</text>
              <text x="160" y="271" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--muted)" font-family="var(--font-special-elite)" font-size="10">m: TIMES THROUGH EACH POINT</text>
              <text x="160" y="293" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--blue)" font-family="var(--font-special-elite)" font-size="10">APPROVED · PLANE CURVES</text>
            </svg>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="nfilm-formulas" aria-hidden="true" data-bleed>
          {labels.map((label) => <span class:list={['nfilm-label', 'nfilm-label--small', { 'nfilm-label--blue': label.blue }]} data-label={label.id}><span set:html={formula(label.tex)} /></span>)}
          <span class="nfilm-label nfilm-status" data-label="status"><span>APPROVED · PLANE CURVES</span></span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="nfilm-subtitles" aria-hidden="true">
        {CUES.map((cue, index) => <p class:list={['nfilm-cue', { 'is-active': index === 0 }]} data-cue={index}><span set:html={subtitle(cue.text)} /><span class="nfilm-citations"> {cue.sources.map((source) => `[${source}]`).join('')}</span></p>)}
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="nfilm-controls" data-script-only>
      <div class="nfilm-buttons">
        <button class="plate-button case-link case-link--tight" type="button" data-play><span data-play-label>Pause</span></button>
        <p class="nfilm-clock"><span data-film-clock>0:00 / {formatTime(FILM_DURATION)}</span></p>
        <button class="plate-button case-link case-link--tight" type="button" data-film-restart>Restart</button>
      </div>
      <label class="visually-hidden" for="nfilm-timeline">Film timeline. Arrow keys move one subtitle at a time.</label>
      <input id="nfilm-timeline" class="nfilm-timeline" data-film-range type="range" min="0" max={FILM_DURATION} step="100" value="0" />
      <div class="nfilm-steps">
        <button class="plate-button case-link case-link--tight" type="button" data-film-previous>Previous</button>
        <p>Step through without motion</p>
        <button class="plate-button case-link case-link--tight" type="button" data-film-next>Next</button>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="visually-hidden" data-film-status aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"></p>
    <details class="nfilm-transcript">
      <summary class="text-link">Read the film as text</summary>
      <ol>{CUES.map((cue) => <li><h3>{cue.title}</h3><p><span set:html={subtitle(cue.text)} /> {cue.sources.map((source) => <> <a class="citation text-link" href={`#source-${source}`}>[{source}]</a></>)}</p></li>)}</ol>
      <p class="nfilm-method">How the film is made. The conic, cubic and nodal cubic are solved at the ten displayed rational pins. Their real zero sets are traced numerically. The nodal cubic has both first derivatives zero at pin 8. A degree <span set:html={formula('d')} /> polynomial has <span set:html={formula('(d+1)(d+2)/2')} /> coefficients; multiplicity <span set:html={formula('m')} /> at one point imposes <span set:html={formula('m(m+1)/2')} /> linear conditions.</p>
      <p class="nfilm-method">The eight plotted minimum degrees are certified at these pins by full column ranks modulo the prime 67,108,859 one degree below each dot. At the displayed degree there are more coefficients than conditions. The strict inequality <span set:html={formula(String.raw`d>m\sqrt r`)} /> is necessary, not sufficient for every integer pair. For example, <span set:html={formula(String.raw`m=6,\ d=19`)} /> lies above the line but has 210 independent conditions on 210 coefficients and no nonzero curve.</p>
      <p class="nfilm-method">The theorem concerns very general points and every multiplicity. This finite calculation through <span set:html={formula('m=8')} /> illustrates it but does not prove it. The moving tenth pin, the pinched model cubic, the exponent triangle and the supposed curve below the line are schematic. Tevelev's notes support the plane-curve theorem; the three companion papers remain unreviewed in the article's dated evidence.</p>
    </details>
  </uruk-curve-budget>
</Plate>

<script>
  import './element';
</script>
